1
00:00:52,889 --> 00:00:55,853
<i>If you want to meet
the person you were talking about earlier,</i>

2
00:00:55,936 --> 00:00:57,439
<i>the key's here, in my pocket.</i>

3
00:01:54,512 --> 00:01:57,643
Don't shoot! Just… Just let me go. Okay? Let me go.

4
00:01:57,727 --> 00:01:59,021
Where is Seong Gi-hun?

5
00:01:59,104 --> 00:02:00,315
Room 410! 410!

6
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,562
Police! Hands above your head, now!

7
00:02:35,844 --> 00:02:39,059
Seong Gi-hun, you are under arrest on suspicion of murder.

8
00:02:40,019 --> 00:02:41,898
You have the right to remain silent.

9
00:02:41,982 --> 00:02:43,276
Anything you say can...

10
00:02:47,117 --> 00:02:48,787
Hold on. Hey, hey! Wait!

11
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:50,081
Who are you?

12
00:02:52,878 --> 00:02:55,717
Hey. Seong Gi-hun. You're him, aren't you?

13
00:02:56,344 --> 00:02:59,433
I work with Mr. Kim, okay? We tracked down your <i>ddakji</i> guy.

14
00:02:59,517 --> 00:03:01,020
My name's Choi Woo-seok.

15
00:03:01,103 --> 00:03:03,191
I'm in all the photos with him, remember?

16
00:03:03,274 --> 00:03:05,320
We texted you from the subway every single day!

17
00:03:05,904 --> 00:03:07,032
Don't you remember?

18
00:03:09,954 --> 00:03:13,002
Listen, okay? I know that we've never met,

19
00:03:13,085 --> 00:03:14,421
at least not in person,

20
00:03:14,505 --> 00:03:17,594
but the boss told me, uh, how much he trusted you.

21
00:03:17,678 --> 00:03:20,308
You were a stand-up guy who voluntarily paid his debts.

22
00:03:20,392 --> 00:03:22,897
He told me that there was nobody else…

23
00:03:24,567 --> 00:03:25,569
Is he dead?

24
00:03:27,698 --> 00:03:29,201
Did you kill him, Mr. Seong?

25
00:03:32,082 --> 00:03:34,545
You fucking son of a bitch!

26
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,845
Fucking hell!

27
00:03:40,724 --> 00:03:44,273
This motherfucker tied us up and killed the boss.

28
00:03:49,283 --> 00:03:52,456
I was sitting there with two rocks like an idiot.

29
00:03:52,539 --> 00:03:54,585
But Boss had scissors and paper.

30
00:03:54,668 --> 00:03:57,549
All he had to do was take back the scissors.

31
00:03:57,633 --> 00:04:00,096
Why the fuck did he pull his hand back?

32
00:04:00,179 --> 00:04:02,768
Why the fuck didn't you just…

33
00:04:02,851 --> 00:04:04,855
OCTOBER 31 MIDNIGHT CLUB HDH

34
00:04:15,919 --> 00:04:19,760
SQUID GAME 2

35
00:04:22,432 --> 00:04:26,774
EPISODE 2 HALLOWEEN PARTY

36
00:04:46,814 --> 00:04:47,816
Excuse me.

37
00:04:49,987 --> 00:04:51,156
Excuse me!

38
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,951
Hey! Wake up!

39
00:04:57,753 --> 00:04:59,214
Roll the window down.

40
00:05:08,775 --> 00:05:10,319
What are you doing out here?

41
00:05:11,906 --> 00:05:13,826
This is where I work, sir.

42
00:05:13,910 --> 00:05:15,496
I have the morning shift.

43
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:18,502
That doesn't mean you can just sleep in your car, you know.

44
00:05:18,586 --> 00:05:20,673
I'll get in trouble if anyone finds out.

45
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:23,888
Haven't I caught you out here before?

46
00:05:23,972 --> 00:05:26,685
It won't happen again. I'll move tomorrow.

47
00:05:27,186 --> 00:05:28,898
Well, this is your final warning.

48
00:05:29,733 --> 00:05:31,988
I'll have to report you if I catch you again.

49
00:05:32,823 --> 00:05:33,866
I understand.

50
00:05:52,863 --> 00:05:54,700
Detective Hwang Jun-ho.

51
00:05:58,123 --> 00:05:59,459
I remember you now.

52
00:06:00,921 --> 00:06:03,092
I talked to you one night at my house, didn't I?

53
00:06:03,885 --> 00:06:05,638
We actually have met twice.

54
00:06:06,390 --> 00:06:09,020
The first time was at your house, and the second time…

55
00:06:10,481 --> 00:06:11,567
Was on the island.

56
00:06:12,444 --> 00:06:15,366
Remember? It was on the night that the fight broke out.

57
00:06:16,368 --> 00:06:18,289
The masks had to step in to shut it down.

58
00:06:19,917 --> 00:06:22,117
Are you saying you worked there as one of their guards?

59
00:06:22,171 --> 00:06:25,136
I infiltrated the island as one of them
so I could find my brother.

60
00:06:25,219 --> 00:06:27,181
How do I know that's not bullshit?

61
00:06:27,265 --> 00:06:29,185
There was a masked man who talked to you,

62
00:06:30,062 --> 00:06:31,690
asked if you knew Hwang In-ho.

63
00:06:32,859 --> 00:06:34,028
<i>Player 456.</i>

64
00:06:34,905 --> 00:06:36,867
Is there a man named Hwang In-ho here?

65
00:06:38,871 --> 00:06:41,335
We don't use our names in this place.

66
00:06:42,504 --> 00:06:43,631
<i>That was me.</i>

67
00:06:44,132 --> 00:06:45,927
Hwang In-ho is my older brother.

68
00:06:50,269 --> 00:06:52,524
Who's that man you killed before I got here?

69
00:06:53,025 --> 00:06:56,657
He's a recruiter. He finds people
and gets them to participate in the game.

70
00:06:57,868 --> 00:06:59,830
And I wasn't the one who fired the gun.

71
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:05,550
We played a game and he just happened to lose.

72
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:10,184
Mr. Seong, are you saying you're still part of that game?

73
00:07:10,768 --> 00:07:13,440
What I want is to stop the game once and for all.

74
00:07:13,524 --> 00:07:14,526
How?

75
00:07:14,609 --> 00:07:16,446
There's someone that I'm gonna find.

76
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:20,246
The son of a bitch who ran the game under Oh Il-nam.

77
00:07:22,291 --> 00:07:23,627
Do you know who he is?

78
00:07:25,673 --> 00:07:27,677
All of the guards called him the Front Man.

79
00:07:27,761 --> 00:07:28,930
You know what he looks like?

80
00:07:31,226 --> 00:07:32,562
No, he…

81
00:07:32,645 --> 00:07:35,818
He always wore a black mask under a hood.

82
00:07:39,075 --> 00:07:40,995
How are you going to find the guy?

83
00:07:42,707 --> 00:07:44,586
He sent me an invitation.

84
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,220
Say you find him.

85
00:07:51,642 --> 00:07:52,644
Then what?

86
00:07:53,771 --> 00:07:54,773
You gonna kill him?

87
00:07:55,733 --> 00:07:58,572
Killing one person isn't gonna put an end to any of this.

88
00:07:59,908 --> 00:08:02,455
Oh Il-nam said something on the night that he died.

89
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:06,296
He said he only decided to create the game
to please his clients.

90
00:08:06,379 --> 00:08:07,381
That's right.

91
00:08:08,342 --> 00:08:10,346
The VIPs. That's what they would call them there.

92
00:08:10,429 --> 00:08:12,224
I saw one of their faces.

93
00:08:13,978 --> 00:08:15,022
Let me go.

94
00:08:16,107 --> 00:08:17,694
We'll find these bastards together.

95
00:08:18,654 --> 00:08:21,368
Seong, listen to me. No cops, please.

96
00:08:21,952 --> 00:08:24,165
The cops never do anything except harass us.

97
00:08:24,248 --> 00:08:25,668
Now suddenly you want to help us?

98
00:08:30,427 --> 00:08:33,851
Sorry about your brother,
but you need to forget about this.

99
00:08:33,934 --> 00:08:35,521
Were you able to forget…

100
00:08:37,358 --> 00:08:39,111
All the people who they murdered?

101
00:08:41,408 --> 00:08:43,579
With the mask on, I saw things you didn't.

102
00:08:44,622 --> 00:08:46,125
Whatever you're trying to do…

103
00:08:48,422 --> 00:08:49,591
I know I can help.

104
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:00,738
Can we please rethink our plan here?

105
00:09:00,821 --> 00:09:03,786
Listen, When I was young, I got scammed
and lost my entire life savings.

106
00:09:03,869 --> 00:09:06,666
I was so pissed, I found the fucker
who did it and roughed him up.

107
00:09:06,750 --> 00:09:08,420
It was nothing. I barely touched the guy.

108
00:09:08,503 --> 00:09:09,965
But the police only went arrested me

109
00:09:10,048 --> 00:09:11,969
and then demanded that <i>I</i> pay him a settlement.

110
00:09:12,052 --> 00:09:13,179
But with what fucking money?

111
00:09:13,263 --> 00:09:15,643
That asshole had already taken everything I had.

112
00:09:15,726 --> 00:09:18,356
What's really fucked up is
I'm the only they threw in the can.

113
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,734
They just let the other guy off.

114
00:09:19,818 --> 00:09:22,197
After that, I'll never trust the police again…

115
00:09:25,997 --> 00:09:26,999
Holy hell.

116
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,669
You really did win.

117
00:09:29,545 --> 00:09:31,800
The game was real. You aren't full of shit.

118
00:09:39,064 --> 00:09:40,818
The money you see here

119
00:09:40,901 --> 00:09:43,261
is the price of the lives of all the people that were lost.

120
00:09:46,496 --> 00:09:49,377
We're gonna take it, and we're gonna use it to fight back.

121
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,216
If you decide to help me,

122
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:55,055
I'll give you all the money you could ever want.

123
00:09:55,639 --> 00:09:58,228
I don't give a shit. I'm not doing this for the money.

124
00:09:58,812 --> 00:10:00,357
No, and neither am I.

125
00:10:01,150 --> 00:10:04,031
That psycho killed the boss and had me watch it.

126
00:10:04,657 --> 00:10:07,914
Boss Kim was like a brother. He officiated my wedding.

127
00:10:08,874 --> 00:10:10,836
I'll track down whoever that fucker answered to,

128
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:13,801
make them play Rock, Paper, Scissors
and shoot all of them dead.

129
00:10:15,053 --> 00:10:17,015
There are armed troops on that island.

130
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:20,564
A couple of pistols
aren't really gonna do us much good there.

131
00:10:24,530 --> 00:10:26,618
This is everything I've collected so far.

132
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,214
Are they real? Mr. Seong, where did you get all of them?

133
00:10:33,298 --> 00:10:35,051
Wow. I'm impressed.

134
00:10:35,135 --> 00:10:37,473
I guess you actually do know what you're doing.

135
00:10:38,266 --> 00:10:40,938
I want you to find a team to come work for us.

136
00:10:41,022 --> 00:10:42,942
Sure, I got it covered.

137
00:10:43,026 --> 00:10:45,906
I already know a crew.
These men are the best in the business.

138
00:10:47,159 --> 00:10:48,537
Wait. Is that a K2?

139
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:51,376
Whoa! Haven't seen these since my military days.

140
00:10:53,129 --> 00:10:55,008
I'm guessing these are black market.

141
00:10:56,093 --> 00:10:57,513
Do you know if they even work?

142
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:12,793
Huh?

143
00:11:23,690 --> 00:11:24,692
Huh?

144
00:11:26,070 --> 00:11:28,450
You can come here to practice anytime you want.

145
00:11:29,619 --> 00:11:30,621
Oh, and…

146
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:35,088
I think you need to quit your current job
if you're gonna work with me.

147
00:11:55,295 --> 00:11:58,343
- Look, here they come.
- Here, hon. Need a boost?

148
00:12:01,056 --> 00:12:02,058
Thank you!

149
00:12:15,084 --> 00:12:16,212
Say thank you, honey.

150
00:12:30,782 --> 00:12:33,371
Shit, I'm roasting. Hey, turn up the AC!

151
00:12:33,454 --> 00:12:36,460
- The unit barely does anything.
- These suits are like ovens.

152
00:12:36,544 --> 00:12:38,590
- Look at me, I'm drenched.
- Is it even on?

153
00:12:38,673 --> 00:12:40,969
- It's so hot.
- Someone talk to management.

154
00:12:41,053 --> 00:12:42,890
They expect us to work in this weather?

155
00:12:42,973 --> 00:12:45,645
- Need something cold.
- Can't wait to get home.

156
00:12:45,729 --> 00:12:47,566
- Mask's soaked.
- AC, please.

157
00:12:47,649 --> 00:12:49,862
- Let's grab a beer.
- Now you're talking.

158
00:12:49,946 --> 00:12:52,200
- I'm in.
- I know a place around the corner.

159
00:12:52,284 --> 00:12:54,162
- I'm exhausted.
- I know, I...

160
00:13:13,534 --> 00:13:16,039
Bunny, here you go.

161
00:13:16,123 --> 00:13:17,334
I drew it for you.

162
00:13:35,328 --> 00:13:36,956
Oh, no. Are you okay, Bunny?

163
00:13:39,503 --> 00:13:41,423
Oh, it is way too hot for this shit.

164
00:13:42,592 --> 00:13:45,097
Why doesn't this fucking pig suit have any ventilation?

165
00:13:45,181 --> 00:13:46,809
Is mine the only one like this?

166
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:57,288
Oh, wait. No, no, no.

167
00:13:57,372 --> 00:13:59,835
Na-yeon!

168
00:13:59,919 --> 00:14:01,589
- Na-yeon!
- Oink, oink!

169
00:14:01,672 --> 00:14:02,674
Na-yeon…

170
00:14:04,303 --> 00:14:07,851
Na-yeon, hey, how many times
have I told you not to wander off?

171
00:14:07,935 --> 00:14:10,607
Daddy!

172
00:14:10,690 --> 00:14:12,193
- Don't cry.
- Daddy!

173
00:14:12,277 --> 00:14:14,531
Sorry, guys. I'll get out of your hair. I'm sorry.

174
00:14:14,615 --> 00:14:16,285
It's all right.

175
00:14:16,368 --> 00:14:18,498
Daddy's got you now. You're okay, sweetie.

176
00:14:24,050 --> 00:14:26,138
I wonder when she got discharged.

177
00:14:26,221 --> 00:14:28,810
Who is she?

178
00:14:29,895 --> 00:14:33,862
Oh, you know the artists who are around
drawing caricatures for the guests?

179
00:14:33,945 --> 00:14:35,991
The man who just left is one of those guys.

180
00:14:36,074 --> 00:14:37,160
The kid's his daughter.

181
00:14:37,661 --> 00:14:39,122
She was in the hospital?

182
00:14:40,667 --> 00:14:44,842
Yeah, well, she has blood cancer.
She needs a bone marrow transplant, but…

183
00:14:45,927 --> 00:14:47,848
Apparently, they're really hard to get.

184
00:14:52,983 --> 00:14:54,152
SANG-WOO'S FISH STORE

185
00:14:54,236 --> 00:14:55,864
Oh, great, Thank you so much.

186
00:14:55,947 --> 00:14:58,077
- Thank you. Have a nice day.
- You too.

187
00:15:05,132 --> 00:15:06,134
Cheol!

188
00:15:06,635 --> 00:15:07,637
Grandma!

189
00:15:08,138 --> 00:15:10,602
- That's fresh.
- They look frozen to me.

190
00:15:13,065 --> 00:15:15,361
- Have you had dinner yet?
- Yeah. I ate.

191
00:15:15,445 --> 00:15:17,240
I got a burger with some friends.

192
00:15:17,323 --> 00:15:18,868
You need more than that.

193
00:15:19,494 --> 00:15:23,419
- I've got some sweet potatoes steaming.
- I'm too full for sweet potatoes.

194
00:15:23,502 --> 00:15:25,089
Then we'll drink some sikhye.

195
00:15:28,345 --> 00:15:30,934
The woman standing next to Sae-byeok in that picture,

196
00:15:31,017 --> 00:15:32,061
that's her mother.

197
00:15:32,646 --> 00:15:35,318
We learned that she was recently released
from a prison camp

198
00:15:35,401 --> 00:15:37,029
in North Hamgyong Province.

199
00:15:38,741 --> 00:15:40,501
You have any idea what kinda shape she's in?

200
00:15:40,578 --> 00:15:43,334
There was an outbreak of tuberculosis in her camp.

201
00:15:43,417 --> 00:15:45,463
She was never treated for it, though.

202
00:15:45,546 --> 00:15:48,218
Trying to move her now isn't really feasible.

203
00:15:48,302 --> 00:15:50,765
I don't care. Please get her mom out of there.

204
00:15:51,266 --> 00:15:54,731
Listen. So I've got Chinese experts
and North Korean experts

205
00:15:54,815 --> 00:15:56,067
hard at work on this.

206
00:15:56,861 --> 00:16:00,743
Once we know she's recovered,
we go and get her across the border.

207
00:16:00,827 --> 00:16:03,499
If the problem is money, I can get you more.

208
00:16:03,582 --> 00:16:04,668
No, no, no.

209
00:16:05,252 --> 00:16:07,465
Last time you gave me more than enough money,

210
00:16:12,767 --> 00:16:15,231
I kind of owe this to Sae-byeok after all.

211
00:16:15,815 --> 00:16:18,320
I'll do everything I can to try and make it happen.

212
00:16:29,801 --> 00:16:30,636
What's this?

213
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:31,638
SANG-WOO'S FISH STORE

214
00:16:31,722 --> 00:16:34,060
That's where Sae-byeok's little brother is.

215
00:16:34,561 --> 00:16:37,275
If for any reason you can't get ahold of me,

216
00:16:38,485 --> 00:16:40,656
I want you to call that number.

217
00:16:41,784 --> 00:16:43,161
Okay. Got it.

218
00:17:02,951 --> 00:17:06,416
Oh, shit. You again? For God's sake!

219
00:17:09,046 --> 00:17:12,720
Why can't you just leave me alone?
Go see another broker like I said.

220
00:17:13,305 --> 00:17:17,021
Everyone else I tried told me that she was dead.

221
00:17:17,104 --> 00:17:19,066
If they all say she's dead, she is.

222
00:17:19,651 --> 00:17:22,072
You can't magically bring your kid back to life.

223
00:17:22,782 --> 00:17:25,454
I thought you said there was a chance she isn't dead.

224
00:17:25,538 --> 00:17:27,709
Actually, what I told you

225
00:17:27,792 --> 00:17:31,550
was that at no point had anyone
reported her body or witnessed her death.

226
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:34,180
That's different than saying she isn't dead.

227
00:17:34,764 --> 00:17:37,061
No one's reported seeing her alive either.

228
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:43,156
Just please look for her one last time, okay?

229
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:45,745
Today, everyone's just throwing cash at me.

230
00:17:47,331 --> 00:17:49,920
I guess it's the universe rewarding my good deeds.

231
00:17:50,003 --> 00:17:51,882
Please look, I'm begging you.

232
00:17:51,965 --> 00:17:54,178
If you need more, I can get it to you.

233
00:17:57,643 --> 00:18:01,025
If the issue were the money,
I would have told you so a while ago.

234
00:18:01,109 --> 00:18:03,071
No-eul, you know how hard I've been working

235
00:18:03,154 --> 00:18:05,492
to try and find some kind of news for you.

236
00:18:06,745 --> 00:18:09,960
I have kids. I feel your pain.
But I've already done everything I can.

237
00:18:10,043 --> 00:18:11,337
Then I know you get it.

238
00:18:13,091 --> 00:18:14,761
This is the last time, I swear.

239
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,934
Listen, I have to be honest with you.

240
00:18:18,602 --> 00:18:20,982
I mean, the baby was one year old.

241
00:18:21,065 --> 00:18:24,113
How could she survive in North Korea without her parents?

242
00:18:24,197 --> 00:18:26,994
Not only that, her mother shot a superior officer

243
00:18:27,077 --> 00:18:30,167
and ran away to the South, just like some traitor who…

244
00:18:36,304 --> 00:18:39,227
Hey, listen, I'm not saying this is your fault, No-eul.

245
00:18:39,728 --> 00:18:42,567
It's just the harsh reality of the situation you're in.

246
00:18:46,575 --> 00:18:50,416
It's awful, I know,
telling you to forget about your kid, but…

247
00:18:52,628 --> 00:18:54,131
You really should.

248
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:57,012
It's the only thing you can do now.

249
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:39,221
Sorry. I'm done. Let me just move the car.

250
00:19:40,015 --> 00:19:41,142
Kang No-eul.

251
00:20:18,675 --> 00:20:19,594
Hey, Mom.

252
00:20:19,677 --> 00:20:22,600
<i>Where are you, sweetie? Are you there yet?</i>

253
00:20:23,602 --> 00:20:24,938
Yeah, Mom, I'm here.

254
00:20:25,021 --> 00:20:29,280
<i>If you can, please take a look around,
see if your brother has dropped by.</i>

255
00:20:30,449 --> 00:20:32,954
<i>I mean, it's the fifth anniversary of her death.</i>

256
00:20:33,037 --> 00:20:36,502
<i>If he's still alive, you'd hope
he would leave his wife some flowers.</i>

257
00:20:58,129 --> 00:21:00,008
There was no sign of him?

258
00:21:00,091 --> 00:21:01,093
No.

259
00:21:04,976 --> 00:21:06,437
That's really it, then.

260
00:21:08,065 --> 00:21:11,739
Your brother truly wants to cut us out of his life.

261
00:21:13,869 --> 00:21:17,083
I really can't believe how long it's been. Can you?

262
00:21:17,167 --> 00:21:19,672
I know that the reason he's gone

263
00:21:20,966 --> 00:21:23,596
is because he still resents me for everything.

264
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:27,229
We were all struggling then.

265
00:21:28,439 --> 00:21:29,525
He knows that.

266
00:21:29,608 --> 00:21:32,280
I just don't want him to think I loved him any less.

267
00:21:32,364 --> 00:21:35,328
Or feel that since I wasn't his birth mother,

268
00:21:35,412 --> 00:21:36,831
I put your needs first.

269
00:21:38,334 --> 00:21:40,422
That's what scares me the most.

270
00:21:40,505 --> 00:21:42,551
Mom, you can't start thinking like that.

271
00:21:43,762 --> 00:21:45,265
In-ho knew that wasn't true.

272
00:21:47,561 --> 00:21:48,646
Still…

273
00:21:50,108 --> 00:21:52,988
He gave you one of his kidneys in order to save your life.

274
00:21:54,450 --> 00:21:58,750
Then when your sister-in-law lay there
in the hospital, suffering and dying,

275
00:22:00,462 --> 00:22:02,549
I didn't do anything to help her.

276
00:22:04,929 --> 00:22:07,267
I wish I could have done something.

277
00:22:11,150 --> 00:22:13,446
I would have given anything to save her.

278
00:22:14,114 --> 00:22:16,285
Even selling off all my organs.

279
00:22:16,953 --> 00:22:18,832
In that case, he'd resent me instead.

280
00:22:21,003 --> 00:22:23,215
A kidney, know how much that's even worth?

281
00:22:23,299 --> 00:22:26,639
He could have paid for all her treatments
if he'd just gone out and sold it.

282
00:22:27,933 --> 00:22:29,733
I should've just died, if you think about it.

283
00:22:29,812 --> 00:22:31,532
After what you put me through don't say it!

284
00:22:31,607 --> 00:22:33,444
You just said the exact same thing!

285
00:22:33,528 --> 00:22:35,198
And I'm tired of hearing it!

286
00:22:36,910 --> 00:22:39,331
She got sick, she died. That was her fate.

287
00:22:40,918 --> 00:22:43,798
You know accepting that bribe was In-ho's decision alone.

288
00:22:44,884 --> 00:22:46,220
We're not responsible for that!

289
00:22:46,303 --> 00:22:48,474
That happened to be how his life turned out!

290
00:22:50,437 --> 00:22:53,317
His actions had consequences. That's how the world works.

291
00:23:37,364 --> 00:23:38,199
RESIGNATION LETTER

292
00:23:38,282 --> 00:23:40,871
Something personal came up and I need to deal with it.

293
00:23:40,954 --> 00:23:43,626
Still, you're just gonna quit on me, out the blue?

294
00:23:45,087 --> 00:23:47,300
It'll be hard to find a replacement.

295
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:48,219
I'm sorry, boss.

296
00:23:48,302 --> 00:23:50,598
No-eul, how the hell do you work in this?

297
00:23:50,682 --> 00:23:54,272
Oh, shit. This one's stuffier than the pig suit was. Fuck.

298
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:58,280
You know, boss, this is why No-eul decided to quit.

299
00:23:58,364 --> 00:24:00,869
Whoever designed these
only thought about what the kids see,

300
00:24:00,952 --> 00:24:03,791
not that they totally suck for the adults wearing them.

301
00:24:03,875 --> 00:24:04,877
Right, No-eul?

302
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:06,088
Team dinner's tonight.

303
00:24:07,173 --> 00:24:09,636
I hope you can come and say good-bye to everyone. Yeah?

304
00:24:09,720 --> 00:24:11,766
You gotta go. Come hang, eat something.

305
00:24:11,849 --> 00:24:15,314
Drink a little soju. Huh?
It'd be a bummer for you to just leave.

306
00:24:15,398 --> 00:24:17,026
Thank you for everything, boss.

307
00:24:23,790 --> 00:24:27,171
Ice-cold right to the very end.

308
00:24:27,255 --> 00:24:28,340
Same as always.

309
00:24:28,424 --> 00:24:31,096
You know, I've worked with her for a little over two years,

310
00:24:31,179 --> 00:24:33,476
but I don't think we ever had a real conversation.

311
00:24:33,559 --> 00:24:37,692
Yeah. I'm not sure how she lasted so long
with that personality.

312
00:25:05,707 --> 00:25:07,585
- Here.
- Tell us what happened?

313
00:25:07,669 --> 00:25:10,049
- I just found her unconscious.
- Na-yeon!

314
00:25:12,470 --> 00:25:13,470
Na-yeon!

315
00:25:16,436 --> 00:25:18,733
- Are you her guardian?
- Yeah, I'm her dad.

316
00:25:18,816 --> 00:25:21,029
Please take her to Seohyeon University Hospital.

317
00:25:38,313 --> 00:25:40,735
Okay, now open wide.

318
00:26:51,585 --> 00:26:53,589
SEOHYEON UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

319
00:27:04,987 --> 00:27:05,989
PARK NA-YEON

320
00:27:06,072 --> 00:27:09,245
Well, there's a new drug
that just got out of the trial phase.

321
00:27:09,329 --> 00:27:14,923
We use it on patients like Na-yeon
with recurrent cancer or a poor prognosis.

322
00:27:15,007 --> 00:27:17,846
The only thing is, it's not covered by insurance yet.

323
00:27:17,929 --> 00:27:20,852
Doctor, I'll figure out a way to get the money somehow.

324
00:27:20,935 --> 00:27:23,273
I'm begging you, please.

325
00:27:23,357 --> 00:27:24,734
Please help my Na-yeon.

326
00:27:24,818 --> 00:27:27,114
Let's make another appointment for tomorrow.

327
00:27:27,198 --> 00:27:30,162
You and I can go over the details.

328
00:28:38,548 --> 00:28:39,550
Whoo!

329
00:28:41,721 --> 00:28:44,644
So these guys, ex-marines, all of them!

330
00:28:44,727 --> 00:28:47,399
And over here, these guys are ex-UDT.

331
00:28:47,483 --> 00:28:50,405
And last, not least, ex-Special Forces.

332
00:28:50,489 --> 00:28:53,286
Now, our friend here, just an ex-traffic cop.

333
00:28:53,370 --> 00:28:56,710
Uh, you saw for yourself,
but they are the cream of the crop.

334
00:28:56,793 --> 00:28:57,879
They get their money,

335
00:28:57,962 --> 00:28:59,883
these guys will do anything.

336
00:28:59,966 --> 00:29:02,137
Oh, um, here's our team leader.

337
00:29:02,221 --> 00:29:05,644
He's bringing us years and years
of experience from all over the world.

338
00:29:05,728 --> 00:29:06,897
The name's Kim.

339
00:29:06,980 --> 00:29:08,775
We need to do things carefully tomorrow.

340
00:29:08,859 --> 00:29:10,821
If, at any point they catch on to our plan,

341
00:29:10,905 --> 00:29:12,241
things could start to fall apart.

342
00:29:12,324 --> 00:29:14,495
Don't worry!

343
00:29:14,579 --> 00:29:17,042
It'll be just the two of us going into the club.

344
00:29:17,125 --> 00:29:19,380
We'll have these guys, ta-da, right outside.

345
00:29:19,463 --> 00:29:21,593
You really think they're gonna let you in?

346
00:29:21,676 --> 00:29:24,766
I already have my outfit ready for tomorrow and everything.

347
00:29:24,849 --> 00:29:26,185
I clean up nice, okay?

348
00:29:26,269 --> 00:29:28,648
- I want to go into the club with you.
- No.

349
00:29:28,732 --> 00:29:30,652
They saw your face when you were on the island.

350
00:29:30,736 --> 00:29:32,531
It's possible they would recognize you.

351
00:29:34,577 --> 00:29:38,668
Do not engage for any reason whatsoever
until you receive the signal from me.

352
00:29:38,752 --> 00:29:39,754
Copy, sir.

353
00:29:43,052 --> 00:29:46,142
If things go south, and something ends up
happening to me tomorrow...

354
00:29:46,225 --> 00:29:48,313
Why would anything happen to you?

355
00:29:49,022 --> 00:29:51,444
We've already got that tracker on you.

356
00:29:51,527 --> 00:29:53,782
So no matter what kind of place those guys take you,

357
00:29:53,865 --> 00:29:55,786
you know we're right there, hot on their heels.

358
00:29:55,869 --> 00:29:57,790
So don't be scared. Don't worry.

359
00:30:25,971 --> 00:30:26,973
<i>Hello?</i>

360
00:30:30,188 --> 00:30:31,232
<i>Hello?</i>

361
00:30:32,108 --> 00:30:33,277
<i>Who is this?</i>

362
00:30:33,361 --> 00:30:34,363
<i>Hello?</i>

363
00:30:37,745 --> 00:30:38,747
<i>Dad?</i>

364
00:30:41,878 --> 00:30:44,216
<i>Dad, is that you?</i>

365
00:30:47,514 --> 00:30:49,435
<i>Ga-yeong, who's on the phone?</i>

366
00:30:49,518 --> 00:30:52,190
<i>I don't know. They won't say anything.</i>

367
00:30:53,067 --> 00:30:54,821
<i>I bet it's a prank call.</i>

368
00:30:54,904 --> 00:30:57,534
<i>Just hang up and come eat. Your soup is getting cold.</i>

369
00:30:58,954 --> 00:30:59,956
<i>Okay.</i>

370
00:31:16,531 --> 00:31:20,956
<i>If you wish to participate,
please state your name and date of birth.</i>

371
00:31:21,875 --> 00:31:23,879
June 25, 1994.

372
00:31:25,006 --> 00:31:26,008
Kang No-eul.

373
00:31:28,513 --> 00:31:30,141
<i>Information confirmed.</i>

374
00:31:30,225 --> 00:31:33,899
<i>Your designated pickup date and location is as follows:</i>

375
00:31:33,982 --> 00:31:36,946
<i>October 31, 2024.</i>

376
00:31:37,030 --> 00:31:41,080
<i>Tancheon parking lot
by the Bongeun Bridge, Songpa-go, Seoul.</i>

377
00:32:04,460 --> 00:32:05,462
Hey!

378
00:32:08,175 --> 00:32:11,933
Whoa, look at all these people.
Why is it so crowded tonight?

379
00:32:12,016 --> 00:32:13,185
OCTOBER 31 MIDNIGHT CLUB HDH

380
00:32:13,269 --> 00:32:16,651
Hold on. Is that today? That's Hall…
It's like an American thing. Hallo…

381
00:32:16,734 --> 00:32:18,696
October 31, Halloween.

382
00:32:18,780 --> 00:32:20,199
Yeah, Halloween.

383
00:32:20,283 --> 00:32:21,702
What are they planning here?

384
00:32:21,786 --> 00:32:24,082
They're up to something. I can feel it.

385
00:32:24,166 --> 00:32:25,919
The guy they call the Front Man…

386
00:32:27,547 --> 00:32:30,345
You said he always wore a gray hood and a black mask?

387
00:32:30,428 --> 00:32:31,555
Yeah.

388
00:32:31,639 --> 00:32:34,478
Ah!

389
00:32:34,561 --> 00:32:37,233
He chose today, so he'd blend in with everybody.

390
00:32:38,110 --> 00:32:40,365
These guys are pretty good, huh? Shit.

391
00:32:46,126 --> 00:32:47,629
- All right, let's go.
- Oh, okay.

392
00:32:52,013 --> 00:32:55,061
Whoa! Wait, wait, wait!
We gotta cover our faces too, right?

393
00:32:56,021 --> 00:32:57,900
Oh, uh, here. How much for this one?

394
00:33:15,894 --> 00:33:18,733
We just made it in! It's underground. Can you hear me okay?

395
00:33:18,816 --> 00:33:21,113
- <i>Yeah, I hear you.</i>
- And the tracker?

396
00:33:22,574 --> 00:33:24,369
Signal's strong. What's it like in there?

397
00:33:24,453 --> 00:33:26,457
<i>It's chaos in here. Total chaos.</i>

398
00:33:26,540 --> 00:33:30,005
Everyone's got a mask on. I can't tell who's who.

399
00:33:30,089 --> 00:33:33,011
Listen, I'll let you know if anything happens.

400
00:33:33,095 --> 00:33:34,097
<i>Okay.</i>

401
00:34:09,543 --> 00:34:12,924
The masks. That's them. They're here.
They're about to head into the club now.

402
00:34:13,509 --> 00:34:17,433
Masks? I just told you,
everyone in this place is wearing a mask.

403
00:34:18,686 --> 00:34:20,857
They're in pink jumpsuits, just like on the island.

404
00:34:22,151 --> 00:34:23,404
Seriously?

405
00:34:35,386 --> 00:34:37,390
What's your deal? Do I know you?

406
00:34:38,267 --> 00:34:40,229
The fuck's wrong with gramps over here?

407
00:34:42,943 --> 00:34:46,157
Whoa! Hey, hold on there, bud.
Wait your turn with everyone else.

408
00:34:46,241 --> 00:34:47,285
Out of the way. Police.

409
00:34:49,623 --> 00:34:51,543
See? You're not the only cop here.

410
00:34:52,963 --> 00:34:55,593
Hey, it's Halloween, dude.
You could've put on a uniform at least.

411
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:56,846
Hey, hey. Whoa!

412
00:34:58,307 --> 00:34:59,476
This look like a toy?

413
00:35:03,860 --> 00:35:05,864
I don't see anyone pink suits!

414
00:35:20,852 --> 00:35:21,937
Oh!

415
00:35:25,236 --> 00:35:28,325
There, I see one. Looks like
he's taking Mr. Seong somewhere.

416
00:35:28,409 --> 00:35:29,619
I'm gonna go after them.

417
00:35:29,703 --> 00:35:32,124
- <i>There's more than one.</i>
- What was that?

418
00:35:32,208 --> 00:35:34,671
- <i>I said I saw two of them!</i>
- What?

419
00:35:42,019 --> 00:35:43,272
Woo-seok, where are you?

420
00:35:44,649 --> 00:35:45,735
Woo-seok, come in!

421
00:36:08,489 --> 00:36:10,159
Woo-seok. Woo-seok, get up!

422
00:36:16,171 --> 00:36:18,717
They've moved out of the building. Everyone, get ready!

423
00:36:19,218 --> 00:36:21,264
You hear that? Lock and load, guys.

424
00:36:21,348 --> 00:36:22,348
Get ready.

425
00:36:53,203 --> 00:36:56,334
They just got into a white limousine.
I want everyone tailing it.

426
00:36:56,919 --> 00:36:59,006
<i>Remember, we need to capture him alive.</i>

427
00:36:59,090 --> 00:37:00,092
Go.

428
00:37:10,821 --> 00:37:12,742
<i>Player 456.</i>

429
00:37:12,825 --> 00:37:14,120
<i>You remember this car?</i>

430
00:37:14,662 --> 00:37:16,249
<i>We spoke in here once before.</i>

431
00:37:20,006 --> 00:37:21,509
So this is the car, huh?

432
00:37:24,098 --> 00:37:26,269
I didn't think it'd be such a cushy limo.

433
00:37:26,352 --> 00:37:28,774
<i>I honestly hoped you would have a good life.</i>

434
00:37:29,275 --> 00:37:32,364
<i>That you'd put the past behind you and find happiness.</i>

435
00:37:33,199 --> 00:37:35,746
It's so touching to hear you really care.

436
00:37:38,669 --> 00:37:40,673
I'm moved, I could almost cry.

437
00:37:40,756 --> 00:37:42,885
<i>You should have gotten on that plane.</i>

438
00:37:43,386 --> 00:37:46,518
<i>That was the best choice you could have made.</i>

439
00:37:46,601 --> 00:37:48,480
You know, I still think about it…

440
00:37:50,567 --> 00:37:52,738
That conversation we had back then.

441
00:37:54,868 --> 00:37:57,999
That's the entire reason I wanted to meet you so badly.

442
00:37:58,082 --> 00:37:59,544
<i>Well, here I am.</i>

443
00:38:00,295 --> 00:38:01,673
<i>Say what you want to say.</i>

444
00:38:02,717 --> 00:38:04,136
<i>What do you want from me?</i>

445
00:38:09,271 --> 00:38:11,025
Stop the game once and for all.

446
00:38:17,788 --> 00:38:20,252
<i>- The game?</i>
- The one you've been playing.

447
00:38:21,254 --> 00:38:24,301
The one that I know is still going on. That game.

448
00:38:24,385 --> 00:38:25,804
<i>We only created it.</i>

449
00:38:26,347 --> 00:38:28,977
<i>All of you chose to participate
in the game of your own free will.</i>

450
00:38:29,061 --> 00:38:30,856
That's a load of shit and you know it.

451
00:38:30,940 --> 00:38:34,822
You take advantage of desperate people
with nowhere else to turn,

452
00:38:35,532 --> 00:38:38,538
and watch as they die one by one to entertain your clients.

453
00:38:39,916 --> 00:38:42,212
You say it's their decision to participate,

454
00:38:43,172 --> 00:38:44,926
like you're trying to sugarcoat it.

455
00:38:45,719 --> 00:38:47,890
You act like you're running a charity event.

456
00:38:48,475 --> 00:38:51,522
<i>Anyone who died was simply a player who lost the game.</i>

457
00:38:52,232 --> 00:38:54,361
<i>Trash eliminated from the competition,</i>

458
00:38:55,196 --> 00:38:59,163
<i>and as we speak, our world is filling up
with more and more trash.</i>

459
00:39:00,415 --> 00:39:01,918
<i>You still don't see, do you?</i>

460
00:39:02,586 --> 00:39:06,051
<i>If the world doesn't change, the game doesn't end.</i>

461
00:39:06,135 --> 00:39:08,264
<i>Do you guys have eyes on the limo?</i>

462
00:39:08,348 --> 00:39:09,851
Yeah, I can see it.

463
00:39:09,934 --> 00:39:12,815
They're on the Seogang Bridge,
heading towards Yeouido. What's next?

464
00:39:12,899 --> 00:39:15,946
Don't do anything yet.
We gotta catch him somewhere less public.

465
00:39:16,030 --> 00:39:17,030
<i>Copy that.</i>

466
00:39:20,873 --> 00:39:23,545
You say this is just the way the world works,

467
00:39:24,255 --> 00:39:27,678
and that we should shut up,
accept it and go on with our lives.

468
00:39:27,762 --> 00:39:30,935
But that's a story you made up to excuse your atrocities.

469
00:39:32,855 --> 00:39:35,736
I know that people are nothing but animals to you.

470
00:39:35,819 --> 00:39:38,909
You think you can buy us
like the racehorses I used to bet on.

471
00:39:41,289 --> 00:39:43,251
<i>You've become more eloquent.</i>

472
00:39:45,171 --> 00:39:49,263
<i>So, your plan is to try and convince the horse owners</i>

473
00:39:49,346 --> 00:39:50,808
<i>to put a stop to the race?</i>

474
00:39:51,977 --> 00:39:53,688
We're still on its tail.

475
00:39:53,772 --> 00:39:56,444
- But something's wrong. This feels off.
- <i>What do you mean?</i>

476
00:39:57,028 --> 00:39:59,283
<i>We just keep circling inner Yeouido.</i>

477
00:39:59,366 --> 00:40:02,498
<i>They might've caught on to us.
All right, stop the limo now.</i>

478
00:40:03,207 --> 00:40:05,170
<i>Copy. Commencing operation.</i>

479
00:40:14,563 --> 00:40:16,442
- Oh, shit.
- What's happening?

480
00:40:17,110 --> 00:40:18,404
One of our tires blew.

481
00:40:18,488 --> 00:40:20,701
Shit. Car Two follow the limo.

482
00:40:20,784 --> 00:40:23,373
<i>- Okay. Back the car up! Hurry!
- Back up, back up.</i>

483
00:40:27,756 --> 00:40:29,176
Sniper. Get down!

484
00:40:30,846 --> 00:40:32,808
Cars One and Two are pinned down.

485
00:40:32,892 --> 00:40:34,687
<i>We can't proceed.</i>

486
00:40:34,770 --> 00:40:38,486
<i>Or maybe you were planning to kidnap me?</i>

487
00:40:39,405 --> 00:40:42,077
I'll follow the limo.

488
00:40:50,176 --> 00:40:51,220
Damn it, I'm hit too.

489
00:40:51,303 --> 00:40:52,389
<i>I'm losing them.</i>

490
00:40:54,351 --> 00:40:55,395
Stop the car.

491
00:40:59,862 --> 00:41:04,037
<i>Did you really think you could
end a game like this with one little gun?</i>

492
00:41:23,367 --> 00:41:24,870
Let me play the game again.

493
00:41:25,371 --> 00:41:26,958
<i>You want to play again?</i>

494
00:41:29,004 --> 00:41:31,300
I want you to send me in there again.

495
00:41:31,383 --> 00:41:34,598
<i>A few moments ago weren't you telling me to stop the game?</i>

496
00:41:34,682 --> 00:41:36,853
Your rich bosses will love it, won't they?

497
00:41:38,523 --> 00:41:40,819
The returning winner who came back to play.

498
00:41:41,821 --> 00:41:43,867
Make it all even more entertaining.

499
00:41:46,038 --> 00:41:47,040
Go ahead,

500
00:41:48,250 --> 00:41:50,296
<i>knock me out and take me to the game.</i>

501
00:41:54,972 --> 00:41:56,099
Why the hesitation?

502
00:41:57,978 --> 00:41:59,439
Are you getting cold feet?

503
00:42:01,318 --> 00:42:03,573
<i>Worried you'll lose to me like Oh Il-nam?</i>

504
00:42:05,368 --> 00:42:08,833
He didn't want to admit it,
not even as he laid there on his deathbed.

505
00:42:10,044 --> 00:42:12,507
He knew someone had come to help that man on the street,

506
00:42:12,591 --> 00:42:14,511
but he refused to look out the window.

507
00:42:15,430 --> 00:42:16,432
It didn't matter.

508
00:42:17,559 --> 00:42:19,563
The moment he drew his last breath,

509
00:42:20,774 --> 00:42:22,485
I could tell that he'd finally…

510
00:42:24,698 --> 00:42:26,159
Realized he'd lost.

511
00:42:28,247 --> 00:42:29,917
<i>Have you seen</i> The Matrix?

512
00:42:30,919 --> 00:42:33,800
<i>They could take the blue pill and live in comfort.</i>

513
00:42:33,883 --> 00:42:36,096
<i>But they take the red pill instead.</i>

514
00:42:36,179 --> 00:42:37,891
<i>Just so they can play the hero.</i>

515
00:42:39,060 --> 00:42:42,567
<i>What about you? Do you think you're a hero too?</i>

516
00:42:42,651 --> 00:42:44,571
<i>Do you think you can change the world?</i>

517
00:42:53,464 --> 00:42:54,758
I can prove it to you.

518
00:42:57,096 --> 00:42:58,140
That you're wrong.

519
00:43:00,520 --> 00:43:02,774
That the world isn't always gonna work…

520
00:43:04,862 --> 00:43:06,156
How you think it should.

521
00:43:09,078 --> 00:43:11,375
<i>If that's what you want, then so be it.</i>

522
00:43:57,175 --> 00:43:58,678
Player 456,

523
00:44:00,055 --> 00:44:01,725
welcome back to the game.

524
00:44:05,608 --> 00:44:08,489
All teams, Plan B is now in effect.

